  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Legislature, executive and judiciary — the three functions of making, executing and interpreting law. The others are chambers, tiers or agencies.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Each organ exercises its own function and may not exercise another's. Control of the courts by the executive and law-making by the judiciary are precisely what the doctrine forbids.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The mutual brakes that keep each organ inside its sphere. The division of functions is separation of powers; the federal division is federalism.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Section 4. Section 5 vests executive power in the President, section 6 vests judicial power in the courts, and section 9 governs amendment.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Section 5 vests executive power in the President, exercised directly or through ministers and public officers. The Federal Executive Council is the body through which much of it is formally transacted.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Section 6 vests judicial power in the courts. The Judicial Service Commission advises on appointments; it does not exercise judicial power.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Making law. Executing is the executive, interpreting is the judiciary, and prosecution belongs to the executive's law officers.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Appropriation is a legislative function: no money leaves the Consolidated Revenue Fund without it. Command of the forces is executive, election petitions are judicial, and currency is the central bank's.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    109 senators — three per state plus one for the FCT — and 360 representatives. Together they make 469, but as two chambers, not one.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Two chambers. Nigeria's is the Senate and the House of Representatives, and the merits claimed for it are second thoughts and better representation of the units.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A second chamber gives second thoughts and represents the states as units. It is more expensive, slower and adds duplication — the standard demerits.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A veto. The National Assembly may override it with a two-thirds majority of each House, which is the check on the check.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Impeachment, followed by removal on a two-thirds vote of the Senate. Recall is the removal of a legislator by the electorate, and censure is a formal disapproval without removal.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The executive executes the law and initiates policy. Law-making is legislative, and interpretation and election petitions are judicial.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Ministers are members of the legislature, and the government survives only while it holds a majority there. A separately elected executive is the presidential model.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Separate election is the defining feature. The President is not a member of the legislature, and ministers are appointed from outside it.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Prime Minister. The monarch or ceremonial president is head of state, the Speaker presides over the lower House, and the Chief Justice heads the judiciary.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Interpretation and adjudication. Making law is legislative, and policy and the budget belong to the executive and legislature respectively.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Judicial review tests validity against the Constitution. Precedent is the binding force of past decisions, delegated legislation is made by a subordinate body, and covering the field decides conflicts between federal and state laws.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    An appeal reviews a decision on the facts or the law; a review tests whether an Act or an executive act is valid at all.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Supreme Court, established by section 230. The Court of Appeal sits below it, and the Federal High Court and the National Industrial Court are courts of first instance in their own fields.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Supreme Court consists of the Chief Justice and twenty-one other justices — a number fixed by the Constitution since 2011. Seven is the quorum for a sitting, which is the option written to catch you.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Tenure and money: a judge may be removed only for inability or misconduct on a Senate address, and salaries are charged to the Consolidated Revenue Fund so they cannot be withheld.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Removal follows an address by the President supported by two-thirds of the Senate, on grounds of inability or misconduct — the mechanism that makes tenure secure.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The magistrate, district, customary and Sharia courts, whose decisions may be appealed upward. The Supreme Court is at the top, not the base.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Federal Judicial Service Commission advises the President on appointments to the federal courts; the National Judicial Council recommends and disciplinarily controls judges. The Bar Association is a professional body.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Section 46 allows a person whose Chapter IV right is breached to apply to a High Court for redress. The legislature legislates, the President and the police are the potential violators.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A minister, council, corporation or agency acting under powers granted by an Act. Law made by the courts is precedent, and a referendum is direct legislation by the people.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Time, expertise, flexibility and emergency are the standard reasons. Delegated legislation does not replace the legislature, the courts or the amending procedure.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Ultra vires — beyond the powers. The courts will declare such a regulation void, which is the main judicial control on delegated legislation.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Publication in the gazette, scrutiny by legislative committees, the power of annulment in the enabling Act, and judicial review are the controls. Armies and referendums have no part in it.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Permanent officials who administer departments and advise ministers. Elected officials and personal staff come and go with a government; the judiciary is a separate organ.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Anonymity is about public responsibility: the minister answers for policy, and the official is not named in the debate. It does not mean that officials are unknown or unaccountable.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Equality before the law is the second limb of Dicey's rule of law. Officials above the law, executive override of courts and judicial policy-making are its opposites.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Confirmation of appointments is a legislative brake on executive appointments. A veto runs the other way, a court's decision is judicial, and an election is the electorate's check.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The prerogative of mercy, exercised on the Council of State's advice. It tempers the judicial outcome but is not a reversal of the conviction.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Passage through both chambers plus assent, or an override of the veto by two-thirds of each House. Introduction, debate and signature by a presiding officer are stages, not the completion.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Adjudication is judicial. Representation, oversight and appropriation are three of the legislature's principal functions.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Ignoring a court order is the practical death of independence; the other three options are the guarantees of it.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The President appoints on the Council's recommendation and the Senate confirms — a procedure that involves the executive and the legislature while leaving the choice to the judges.
  ]

]

